          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            The notion of
            %em Klein geometry
            goes back to
          %ul
            %li#Klein1872
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Felix+Klein"}> Felix Klein
                ,
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vergleichende+Betrachtungen+%C3%BCber+neuere+geometrische+Forschungen"} Vergleichende Betrachtungen über neuere geometrische Forschungen
                (1872) Mathematische Annalen volume 43, pages 63–100 1893 (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01446615"}> doi:10.1007/BF01446615
                )
              %p English translation by M. W. Haskell:
              %p
                %em> A comparative review of recent researches in geometry
                , Bull. New York Math. Soc. 2, (1892-1893), 215-249. (
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/bulletin-of-the-american-mathematical-society-new-series/volume-2/issue-10/A-comparative-review-of-recent-researches-in-geometry/bams/1183407629.full"}> euclid:1183407629
                , LaTeX version retyped by Nitin C. Rughoonauth:
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0807.3161"} arXiv:0807.3161
          %p
            in the context of what came to be known as the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Erlangen+program"} Erlangen program
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              Vladimir Kisil,
              %em Erlangen Programme at Large: An Overview
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1106.1686"}> arXiv:1106.1686
              )
          %p
            Monograph account in the broader context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+geometry"} Cartan geometry
          %ul
            %li#Sharpe97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+W.+Sharpe"}> Richard W. Sharpe
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Shapes Fantastic: Klein Geometries
              = succeed "," do
                %em Differential geometry – Cartan’s generalization of Klein’s Erlagen program
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 166
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/9780387947327"} ISBN:9780387947327
          %h3#ReferencesAlternativeTerminology Alternative terminology
          %p
            Beware that some authors say “Kleinian geometry” for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+geometry"} pseudo-Riemannian geometry
            of signature
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
